# App modes — vocabulary

**Full spec:** `docs/concepts/MODES.md`

When the user says **home**, **home view**, **world view**, or **viewer**, they mean **`route: viewer`** (`#/`, `#/home`) — the main 3D scene with animations.

**Creator** = **`route: creator`** (`#/creator/...`). Submodes (also “Creator.Wardrobe” etc.):

| Say this | `editMode` / hash segment |
|----------|---------------------------|
| Creator.Wardrobe, wardrobe mode | `wardrobe` → `#/creator/wardrobe` |
| Creator.3D, 3D edit | `3d` → `#/creator/3d` |
| Creator.2D, 2D / pixel edit | `2d` → `#/creator/2d` |

**Preview** = **`route: preview`** (`#/preview`) — separate from Home/Creator; see `MODES.md`.

**Code:** `getRouteInfo` / `applyRoute` in `src/main.ts`; `setEditMode` in `src/creator.ts`; `document.body.dataset.route` and `dataset.editMode`.

