## “Layers” — use a qualifier (the word is overloaded)

| Say this | Meaning | Code / UI |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| **Wardrobe layer** | A row in the Creator.Wardrobe **tree** (including composites like `top`, `jacketGroup`, and atomics like `head`). Drives camera presets, which **library** is shown, and (with focused creation) solo mapping into skin layers. | `WardrobeLayerKey`, tree in `src/creator/wardrobeLayers.ts`; selection + hover in wardrobe UI |
| **Skin layer** / **paint layer** | One of the **eight** Minecraft skin regions (visibility, lock, 2D mask): `hat`, `head`, `body`, `arms`, `jacket`, `sleeves`, `pants`, `legs`. | `LayerKey` / `layer3DVisible` in `src/skin`, **`#creator-layers-panel`** (Creator.2D / Creator.3D only) |
| **Model layer** / **mesh part** | The corresponding **3D mesh** on the character (show/hide with skin-layer visibility). | `applyCreatorLayerVisibility` and mesh naming in `src/skin` / viewer — same part names as skin layers |

When discussing behavior, prefer **wardrobe layer** vs **skin layer** (or **paint layer**) vs **model part** so agents don’t mix solo/camera/UI (wardrobe) with the 8-region panel (skin) with Three.js meshes (model).

